II. MATERIALS AND METHODS
A. Dataset
This study utilizes the Parkinson’s Disease Smartwatch (PADS) dataset, a publicly available dataset of smartwatch sensor data collected by University Hospital Mu ̈nster in Germany [15]. The dataset includes inertial measurement unit (IMU) recordings from 469 participants—comprising individuals with Parkinson’s disease (PD), those with other movement disorders (differential diagnoses, DD), and healthy controls (HC). The demographic characteristics are summarized in Table I.
